---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
		<img src="/workspaces/johntwyghyde.com/sca-blog/src/assets/Logo_Chop.webp">
			<h1>John "Twyg" Hyde</h1>
			<p>John Hyde is an artist whose creative spirit is inspired by nature and emotion evoked through the transformative powers of both the creation and performance of his pieces.</p>
<p>With a healthy respect for the level of emotion that can be felt while viewing unsettling pieces, he attempts to hone his work to help the viewer safely journey to a place where we can explore the darker side of ourselves. The creations are carefully crafted from traditional and innovative tools so that we can, through conscientious creation, and then sacred play, perhaps discover a path to knowing ourselves better.</p>
<p>Are you here from the <a href="https://sca.org">Society from Creative Anachronism?</a> Please see my SCA blog. While adjacent to my art practice, the SCA allows me to study historic art and use those influences in my own art practice.</p>
			<p>
				This template comes with a few integrations already configured in your
				<code>astro.config.mjs</code> file. You can customize your setup with&nbsp;
				<a href="https://astro.build/integrations">Astro Integrations</a> to add tools like Tailwind,
				React, or Vue to your project.
			</p>
			<p>Here are a few ideas on how to get started with the template:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Edit this page in <code>src/pages/index.astro</code></li>
				<li>Edit the site header items in <code>src/components/Header.astro</code></li>
				<li>Add your name to the footer in <code>src/components/Footer.astro</code></li>
				<li>Check out the included blog posts in <code>src/content/blog/</code></li>
				<li>Customize the blog post page layout in <code>src/layouts/BlogPost.astro</code></li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Have fun! If you get stuck, remember to <a href="https://docs.astro.build/">read the docs</a>&nbsp;
				or <a href="https://astro.build/chat">join us on Discord</a> to ask questions. <a href="/testTheme.astro">testTheme</a>
			</p>
			<p>
				Looking for a blog template with a bit more personality? Check out&nbsp;
				<a href="https://github.com/Charca/astro-blog-template">astro-blog-template</a>&nbsp;
				by <a href="https://twitter.com/Charca">Maxi Ferreira</a>.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
